Replace reallocarray() with realloc() in femu's QEMU compat layer.

reallocarray() was only added to glibc in 2.26, but the simbricks-femu-sim-bin
recipe deliberately targets an older sysroot (glibc 2.17) for broad,
arch-independent compatibility. There the symbol is absent and the femu link
fails with "undefined reference to reallocarray". The scatter-gather list grows
one entry at a time, so the array size can never overflow size_t; a plain
realloc() with the multiplication done explicitly is equivalent in practice.

diff --git a/femu/qemu-compat/wrapper-qemu.c b/femu/qemu-compat/wrapper-qemu.c
--- a/femu/qemu-compat/wrapper-qemu.c
+++ b/femu/qemu-compat/wrapper-qemu.c
@@ -579,7 +579,8 @@

 void qemu_sglist_add(QEMUSGList *qsg, dma_addr_t base, dma_addr_t len)
 {
-    void *new_sg = reallocarray(qsg->sg, qsg->nsg + 1, sizeof(*qsg->sg));
+    void *new_sg = realloc(qsg->sg,
+                           (size_t)(qsg->nsg + 1) * sizeof(*qsg->sg));
     if (!new_sg)
         abort();

